{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>שתו</b> — the tav has a dagesh, for it is from the doubled-roots. They explain that \"their mouth\" is as though in the heavens, meaning their decrees cannot be reversed, and the organ speaking thus is from the earth — this is the sense of \"and their tongue walks in the earth.\" But the correct interpretation in my eyes: \"their mouth has set [its place] in the heavens\" — they speak of HaShem and His angels, and their tongue is like spies who walk the earth to speak and report a rumor or defect, a thing found among the righteous, and the sense of \"walks\" is as though it goes about to hear defects."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 73, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:10.729259967Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}